* =====================================================================================================
* sleep_current__bq25180.lib -- BQ25180 1S charger / power path, battery-only and ship mode, DC model
*
* Part      : Texas Instruments BQ25180YBGR (base board U1), VIN = 0 (no USB)
* Datasheet : https://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/bq25180.pdf  (SLUSE99C, September 2021, revised January 2023)
*
* Battery-only mode (SC_BQ25180_BATT, BATFET on, push-button function enabled = EN_PUSH 1, firmware §13):
*   IQ_BAT   4 uA typ / 5 uA max with push-button function enabled, VIN < VUVLO, VBAT 3.6 V, 0..85 C
*            (Table 7.5 IQ_BAT, second row). The first row (3 uA typ / 3.5 uA max) has the push button off.
*   ITS      the TS/MR current source is pulsed in battery-only mode: ITSMR 60 uA typ (Table 7.5, "Battery
*            only mode") for tTS_DUTY_ON 4 ms every tTS_DUTY_ON + tTS_DUTY_OFF = 4 + 196 ms (Table 7.6)
*            -> 1.2 uA average, sourced from BAT out of the TS/MR pin into the external NTC/button network.
*            IQ_BAT is a BAT-pin figure with the push button on, so it is taken to contain this average; the
*            model therefore splits it: core BAT->GND = IQ_BAT - 1.2 uA, plus the 1.2 uA TS/MR source.
*   VTS_CLAMP 2.8 V typ active clamp on TS/MR (Table 7.5) -- keeps the node bounded if TS/MR is open.
*   RON_BAT  55 mohm typ / 90 mohm max BATFET (Table 7.5)
*   ILKG     SCL, SDA, /INT high-level leakage <= 1 uA max each (Table 7.5, I2C and logic pins); no typical
*            value -> 0 in the typical corner, 1 uA in the max corner (sinks into the pin when pulled high).
*
* Ship mode (SC_BQ25180_SHIP, EN_RST_SHIP = 10, wake on button or adapter):
*   IBAT_SHIP 3.2 uA typ / 4.5 uA max, VBAT 3.6 V, push-button function enabled (average current), 0..85 C
*            (Table 7.5). Split the same way: core = IBAT_SHIP - 1.2 uA, plus the pulsed TS/MR source.
*   SYS pull-down: "enabled once the device enters shipmode and after disconnecting the BATFET" (§8.3.4.1
*            Table 8-2); RSYS_PD 25 ohm typ at VSYS = 3.6 V (Table 7.5 "SYS pull down resistance").
*            [verifier: the earlier "not specified, 1 kohm assumed" was wrong; it only sets VSYS = 0 either way]
*   ILKG     SCL / SDA / /INT leakage as in battery-only mode (the pins exist in ship mode too; their pull-ups
*            sit on the unpowered +3V3, so this is 0 in practice -- it also keeps those nodes in the deck).
*   BATFET off: open.
*
* MAXC = 0 typical, 1 datasheet maximum. No temperature data inside 0..85 C beyond the max -> constant.
* NOT modelled: VIN present (charging / adapter mode), BUVLO / VBATPOR thresholds, watchdog, the pulse shape
*   of the TS source (averaged), BATFET off-state leakage (not specified), IQ dependence on VBAT (spec at 3.6 V).
* =====================================================================================================
.subckt SC_BQ25180_BATT in sys bat tsmr scl sda intn vss params: MAXC=0
.param iqbat = {MAXC > 0.5 ? 5u : 4u}
.param its   = {60u * 4m / (4m + 196m)}
.param ron   = {MAXC > 0.5 ? 90m : 55m}
.param ilkg  = {MAXC > 0.5 ? 1u : 0}
Rbatfet bat sys {ron}
Iqcore bat vss DC {iqbat - its}
Its bat tsmr DC {its}
Vclamp nclamp vss 2.8
Dclamp tsmr nclamp DBQCLAMP
Bscl scl vss I = 'ilkg * tanh(v(scl,vss)/0.1)'
Bsda sda vss I = 'ilkg * tanh(v(sda,vss)/0.1)'
Bint intn vss I = 'ilkg * tanh(v(intn,vss)/0.1)'
.model DBQCLAMP D(IS=1e-14 N=1)
.ends SC_BQ25180_BATT

.subckt SC_BQ25180_SHIP in sys bat tsmr scl sda intn vss params: MAXC=0
.param iship = {MAXC > 0.5 ? 4.5u : 3.2u}
.param its   = {60u * 4m / (4m + 196m)}
.param ilkg  = {MAXC > 0.5 ? 1u : 0}
Iqcore bat vss DC {iship - its}
Its bat tsmr DC {its}
Vclamp nclamp vss 2.8
Dclamp tsmr nclamp DBQCLAMPS
Rsyspd sys vss 25
Bscl scl vss I = 'ilkg * tanh(v(scl,vss)/0.1)'
Bsda sda vss I = 'ilkg * tanh(v(sda,vss)/0.1)'
Bint intn vss I = 'ilkg * tanh(v(intn,vss)/0.1)'
.model DBQCLAMPS D(IS=1e-14 N=1)
.ends SC_BQ25180_SHIP
